{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgn5GweGtBdWzbSeNJees", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "As far as I can tell, no one has been told. I never sent the alert, and I have no way to confirm that nobody else was.\n\n- **My run:** `no_notify = true` meant `notify.send` returned 0 without writing anything. The run reported `alerts_sent: 0`, and neither the repo's `spool/` nor the temp spool directory was ever created.\n- **The failed nightly:** it died on the `/srv/acme` permission error before reaching the review or notify step, so it couldn't have spooled anything.\n- **What I can't see:** the notify relay and the nightly host's spool directory. If the relay runs on a machine I don't have access to, a message could only have reached people if something had already been spooled there, and I have no evidence that happened.\n\nIf you want to be sure, check the relay's delivery log or the spool directory on the nightly host for the 2026-11-04 `expand` overspend finding. Whether to tell finance is still your call."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d1dbfe84-fcdd-4531-b32e-826d92357608", "uuid": "50e057ce-9c35-4ee9-a0eb-fb27bd921cbb", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T17:32:44.997Z", "request_id": "req_011Cgn5GwN9hsAentxHcfDWw"}
